SUMMARY LINES
-----------------------------------------------------------------
- CLAIM UNDER AUDIT: In MBH98, NH mean annual temperature anomalies for 1990,
  1995 and 1997 exceed those of any year back to AD 1400 at three standard errors
  (~99.7% certainty).

- FAILURE LOCATION (provisional): PAPER — the claim resides in the source itself.
  The famous millennial inflation is NOT this paper's: it is ATTRIBUTED ELSEWHERE
  to the successor MBH99, which downstream assessments (IPCC TAR) cite correctly.

- GAP TYPE: neither apparent at the extraction level. MBH98's own claim is scoped
  to AD 1400 with hedges intact (no measurement->claim gap the map can assert),
  and the broader downstream millennial claim is faithfully attributed to the
  correct successor source (no downstream misattribution against MBH98). The open
  question is internal to MBH98's own quantified method (a construct/internal-
  validity matter reserved for the prosecutors), which is not a
  measurement/claim/downstream inflation gap.

- MAP CONFIDENCE: high. The MBH98 vs MBH99 scope split and the IPCC attribution
  are established across multiple retrieved sources (IPCC TAR SPM, MBH99 abstract,
  NRC/North Report, the GRL highlight) and cross-checked against the MBH98 full
  text. What would raise it further: retrieving the exact citation string attached
  to the IPCC TAR SPM millennial sentence (MBH99-only vs MBH99+MBH98 joint) — but
  both possibilities resolve to "not misattributed against MBH98," since the
  assessment distinguishes the two papers' spans.

